WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.230
Instructor: All right, so now it's time

00:01.230 --> 00:02.790
to get some practice on your own

00:02.790 --> 00:06.780
with the GitHub basics, creating GitHub repositories,

00:06.780 --> 00:10.230
setting up remotes, pushing, that sort of thing.

00:10.230 --> 00:13.260
So, nothing crazy here, but really the bread and butter

00:13.260 --> 00:15.810
of working with GitHub is just getting your code

00:15.810 --> 00:19.890
up on GitHub, and then as we'll soon see, getting code down,

00:19.890 --> 00:22.320
pulling down from GitHub, which we haven't yet learned.

00:22.320 --> 00:24.480
Anyway, as always, for these exercises

00:24.480 --> 00:27.570
you can find the link to get to these instructions

00:27.570 --> 00:29.700
as a resource with this video.

00:29.700 --> 00:33.180
So, I recommend you open that up and probably, like always,

00:33.180 --> 00:35.310
just pause this video and read the instructions.

00:35.310 --> 00:38.310
If you have questions, come back to this video.

00:38.310 --> 00:40.380
So, the core idea here is that you're going

00:40.380 --> 00:43.290
to make a new repository locally on your computer.

00:43.290 --> 00:46.620
Then you'll go to GitHub and make a GitHub repository,

00:46.620 --> 00:48.870
and then you'll connect the two.

00:48.870 --> 00:52.560
Then after that you'll make a file

00:52.560 --> 00:56.010
called favorites.txt, an empty file.

00:56.010 --> 00:58.860
You'll save and you'll make your first commit.

00:58.860 --> 01:00.600
Now, this part is optional

01:00.600 --> 01:02.880
if you want to go with main instead of master.

01:02.880 --> 01:05.880
I'm gonna be using main just to be consistent in this file,

01:05.880 --> 01:08.310
but if you choose to stay with master

01:08.310 --> 01:10.650
then just sub that in wherever you see main.

01:10.650 --> 01:13.710
So, you'll make a new file, favorites.txt, leave it empty,

01:13.710 --> 01:15.630
make your first commit on the main branch.

01:15.630 --> 01:18.090
Then push up that main branch to GitHub,

01:18.090 --> 01:21.510
so make sure that you see your empty file on GitHub.

01:21.510 --> 01:24.840
Then the next bit is to make two branches, a foods branch

01:24.840 --> 01:28.740
and a movies branch, both based on the main branch.

01:28.740 --> 01:30.553
Then switch to the foods branch,

01:30.553 --> 01:32.995
add three or more of your favorite foods to the file,

01:32.995 --> 01:34.527
add and commit your changes.

01:34.527 --> 01:36.135
Then switch to the movies branch,

01:36.135 --> 01:37.506
add three or more of your favorite movies

01:37.506 --> 01:40.695
to the favorites file, add and commit your changes.

01:40.695 --> 01:43.290
Then push up your foods branch to GitHub,

01:43.290 --> 01:46.170
and make sure you see it on GitHub if you refresh the page.

01:46.170 --> 01:47.910
And then do the same thing for the movies branch,

01:47.910 --> 01:49.500
push up the movies branch.

01:49.500 --> 01:51.330
And then we get to this step

01:51.330 --> 01:54.000
where I'd like you to merge the foods branch,

01:54.000 --> 01:55.350
let me fix the highlighting.

01:55.350 --> 01:56.430
Okay, there we go.

01:56.430 --> 02:00.090
So, you'll merge the foods branch into the main branch,

02:00.090 --> 02:01.740
and then you'll merge the movies branch

02:01.740 --> 02:02.910
into the main branch.

02:02.910 --> 02:04.860
So, you should now have, after this step,

02:04.860 --> 02:08.490
a favorites file that contains both your favorites movies,

02:08.490 --> 02:09.690
both your favorite movies

02:09.690 --> 02:13.470
and your favorite foods in the same file, favorites.txt,

02:13.470 --> 02:15.180
on the main branch.

02:15.180 --> 02:17.070
So, now the main branch has changed,

02:17.070 --> 02:18.510
GitHub doesn't have that.

02:18.510 --> 02:21.060
So, push up the latest work from that main branch,

02:21.060 --> 02:22.860
push it up to GitHub.

02:22.860 --> 02:24.450
So, that's the basic steps, right?

02:24.450 --> 02:27.660
Make a repo, go on GitHub, make a repo, connect the two.

02:27.660 --> 02:30.810
Then push up your first little commit on the main branch,

02:30.810 --> 02:33.150
make two branches, do some work on both of them,

02:33.150 --> 02:34.950
push each of them up individually,

02:34.950 --> 02:36.600
and then merge those branches locally

02:36.600 --> 02:39.720
into the main branch and push the main branch up again.

02:39.720 --> 02:42.780
So, please give it a shot on your own

02:42.780 --> 02:44.700
unless you are very comfortable with GitHub.

02:44.700 --> 02:46.860
I don't know why you'd be watching this video anyway,

02:46.860 --> 02:49.170
but I know it's not the most exciting possible.

02:49.170 --> 02:50.400
I mean, none of these exercises

02:50.400 --> 02:52.170
are gonna knock your socks off,

02:52.170 --> 02:54.600
but very important basic workflow.

02:54.600 --> 02:55.920
So, I'll go ahead and do it.

02:55.920 --> 02:58.370
I'll make a new repository locally on my machine.

02:59.250 --> 03:00.180
Let's do it in a folder.

03:00.180 --> 03:02.280
I'll call this Favorites.

03:02.280 --> 03:06.450
I'll cd into it, and check that I'm not in a repo.

03:06.450 --> 03:08.430
I'll init, a new repo.

03:08.430 --> 03:10.170
Okay, and then I'll go ahead

03:10.170 --> 03:12.120
and make my new GitHub repository,

03:12.120 --> 03:16.350
so go to github.com, click the plus, New repository,

03:16.350 --> 03:21.350
and I'll just call this one gh-favorites-exercise.

03:23.280 --> 03:24.750
Name it whatever you'd like.

03:24.750 --> 03:25.950
I'll keep it public.

03:25.950 --> 03:27.030
If you wanna take a look,

03:27.030 --> 03:28.530
there's not really gonna be much to look at,

03:28.530 --> 03:30.450
but you're welcome to.

03:30.450 --> 03:31.900
And then I'm gonna create it.

03:33.360 --> 03:36.210
And then the next step is to connect my local repo

03:36.210 --> 03:40.320
to the GitHub repo, which really just means add this remote.

03:40.320 --> 03:41.823
So, I'm gonna add that remote.

03:43.410 --> 03:46.860
And then optionally rename my master branch to main,

03:46.860 --> 03:48.510
we can just copy that.

03:48.510 --> 03:49.980
Assuming that we're on the master branch,

03:49.980 --> 03:52.590
or in this case we're not even on a branch yet,

03:52.590 --> 03:55.350
so I will need to make that master branch

03:55.350 --> 03:58.530
or I will need to do some work, but then I can rename it.

03:58.530 --> 04:00.510
So, as you can see, I'm not even on a branch yet.

04:00.510 --> 04:02.880
I don't have any commits, so there's no branch reference.

04:02.880 --> 04:05.880
But I'll just save that line for just a moment

04:05.880 --> 04:07.590
because next we're going to make

04:07.590 --> 04:10.350
a new file called favorites.txt.

04:10.350 --> 04:12.600
We'll leave it empty and make our first commit.

04:12.600 --> 04:16.740
So, touch favorites.txt, then we'll add it,

04:16.740 --> 04:18.270
so git add favorites.

04:18.270 --> 04:20.970
And we'll commit, just do something like

04:20.970 --> 04:23.043
add empty favorites file.

04:24.210 --> 04:26.730
Okay, so now we see master there,

04:26.730 --> 04:29.460
and I'm gonna rename that to main, right?

04:29.460 --> 04:32.910
So, I type git status, we see on branch main.

04:32.910 --> 04:33.780
If I type git branch

04:33.780 --> 04:35.490
we don't have the master branch anymore.

04:35.490 --> 04:38.280
So, if you want to go with main that's how you do it.

04:38.280 --> 04:41.640
Next, we need to push up this main branch to GitHub.

04:41.640 --> 04:44.610
Right now nothing is up here, it's just empty.

04:44.610 --> 04:48.840
So, git push origin, that's the name of our remote.

04:48.840 --> 04:51.510
And you can always check, git remote -v,

04:51.510 --> 04:54.150
it is origin if you just copied and pasted from GitHub.

04:54.150 --> 04:59.150
So, git push origin, and then main is my branch.

05:00.000 --> 05:03.240
And if I refresh here we should see that empty file,

05:03.240 --> 05:04.470
and there it is.

05:04.470 --> 05:08.250
Okay, so next step we need to create two branches,

05:08.250 --> 05:09.840
foods and movies.

05:09.840 --> 05:14.553
So, git branch foods, git branch movies,

05:15.390 --> 05:19.080
or I could do git switch -c or git checkout -b.

05:19.080 --> 05:20.130
I can switch to one of them,

05:20.130 --> 05:24.900
so I'm gonna switch to foods, if I can spell that.

05:24.900 --> 05:27.090
And then add two, or what'd I say,

05:27.090 --> 05:30.600
three of my favorite foods to the favorites file.

05:30.600 --> 05:32.253
So, let me open this file.

05:34.590 --> 05:37.050
And what are my favorite foods?

05:37.050 --> 05:38.850
I did not think through this at all.

05:40.020 --> 05:42.360
Well, one of them would have to be peppermint ice cream.

05:42.360 --> 05:45.870
Not just mint chip, it has to be peppermint ice cream.

05:45.870 --> 05:47.580
It's not that common anymore.

05:47.580 --> 05:49.780
I used to have it around Christmas as a kid.

05:51.060 --> 05:52.230
What else?

05:52.230 --> 05:53.970
Man, I'm gonna sound like such a fatty

05:53.970 --> 05:58.020
if I just say my honest favorites (laughs), soft pretzels.

05:58.020 --> 05:59.520
Oh, I love soft pretzels.

05:59.520 --> 06:03.930
And then I feel like I need to just lie.

06:03.930 --> 06:05.190
How about celery?

06:05.190 --> 06:07.320
Yeah, I just love celery.

06:07.320 --> 06:10.110
All right, so now I need to add and commit this

06:10.110 --> 06:12.000
on the foods branch.

06:12.000 --> 06:16.740
So, git add favorites, git commit -m

06:16.740 --> 06:19.533
add favorite foods, not doods.

06:21.030 --> 06:23.280
And then that's it.

06:23.280 --> 06:25.530
I could skip ahead and just push it up,

06:25.530 --> 06:28.530
but I'm gonna now switch to the movies branch.

06:28.530 --> 06:30.720
Git switch to movies and add three

06:30.720 --> 06:32.220
of my favorite movies in here.

06:32.220 --> 06:35.070
If you've seen any of my other courses you probably know,

06:35.070 --> 06:37.890
or at least maybe you might remember

06:37.890 --> 06:39.150
my favorite movie is "Amadeus."

06:39.150 --> 06:42.300
I think I say that far too often in my courses.

06:42.300 --> 06:44.160
Great film, you gotta watch it if you haven't seen it.

06:44.160 --> 06:46.470
And if you don't like it I get it, it's not for everyone.

06:46.470 --> 06:49.350
But anyway, how about "The Fifth Element,"

06:49.350 --> 06:51.060
that's another one I like.

06:51.060 --> 06:54.150
Not necessarily, this is not top three movies, not in order.

06:54.150 --> 06:55.290
It doesn't matter, okay?

06:55.290 --> 06:57.300
It doesn't matter at all.

06:57.300 --> 06:58.200
What else?

06:58.200 --> 07:00.487
Hmm, here's a fun one I liked quite a bit,

07:00.487 --> 07:04.230
"Captain Fantastic," Viggo Mortensen.

07:04.230 --> 07:06.427
Sure, we'll say those are my favorites, not quite.

07:06.427 --> 07:08.583
"Amadeus" though, yeah, always number one.

07:09.540 --> 07:13.410
Okay, so now I'm gonna add those changes, git add favorites,

07:13.410 --> 07:18.090
git commit add three of my fav movies.

07:18.090 --> 07:20.520
Okay, and then we get to this step,

07:20.520 --> 07:23.160
push up the foods branch to GitHub.

07:23.160 --> 07:26.940
So, I can just do git push, my remote origin,

07:26.940 --> 07:28.893
and then the name of the branch, foods.

07:29.940 --> 07:32.100
I don't need to be on the foods branch,

07:32.100 --> 07:35.850
and I'll refresh and we should see a new branch.

07:35.850 --> 07:36.683
There it is.

07:36.683 --> 07:38.490
And we wanna verify we see our foods,

07:38.490 --> 07:41.460
whatever you put they show up here, right?

07:41.460 --> 07:43.650
And I'm, currently I was looking at that file,

07:43.650 --> 07:45.090
so that's why I saw this view.

07:45.090 --> 07:46.950
You'd probably see this.

07:46.950 --> 07:48.960
Okay, now push up the movies branch,

07:48.960 --> 07:53.257
git push origin movies, and refresh.

07:57.660 --> 08:01.620
Okay, we see the movies branch, and there we are.

08:01.620 --> 08:03.750
We see favorites and it has my favorite,

08:03.750 --> 08:05.670
or some of my favorite movies.

08:05.670 --> 08:09.090
Then finally, merge the food branch into the main branch.

08:09.090 --> 08:10.953
So, I'm gonna switch to main,

08:12.480 --> 08:14.610
and then I'll just show you my favorites file

08:14.610 --> 08:15.633
is empty right now.

08:16.500 --> 08:21.480
And I'm gonna merge in foods, so git merge foods,

08:21.480 --> 08:23.400
and that's just a fast forward.

08:23.400 --> 08:25.200
Okay, that's the easy part.

08:25.200 --> 08:27.990
Then I need to merge the movies branch into main.

08:27.990 --> 08:29.580
Now, this won't be a fast forward

08:29.580 --> 08:31.680
because now there's commits on the main branch

08:31.680 --> 08:33.180
that the movies branch does not have.

08:33.180 --> 08:38.180
So, git merge and then movies, and we get a lovely conflict.

08:38.850 --> 08:41.820
I'm just gonna select Accept Both Changes,

08:41.820 --> 08:43.170
and there we go.

08:43.170 --> 08:44.790
We'll just leave it like this.

08:44.790 --> 08:46.680
I could put a little heading I guess if I wanted

08:46.680 --> 08:50.310
that said movies here, meh, I'll just leave it like that.

08:50.310 --> 08:52.980
Anyway, I'm gonna resolve the conflict like I just did.

08:52.980 --> 08:57.780
I'm gonna add favorites, and then I'll make my commit here.

08:57.780 --> 08:59.190
What should I do?

08:59.190 --> 09:00.570
Let's just clear.

09:00.570 --> 09:05.570
Git commit, merge movies and foods into main, okay?

09:08.640 --> 09:11.850
And then finally I need to push that up, right?

09:11.850 --> 09:14.370
So, I don't have that latest commit

09:14.370 --> 09:16.083
on the main branch on GitHub.

09:17.088 --> 09:20.670
If I go to it it's just an empty file, very sad.

09:20.670 --> 09:24.060
Now, it's just as simple as git push,

09:24.060 --> 09:26.220
now I didn't use -u in the previous,

09:26.220 --> 09:27.720
when I first pushed the first time.

09:27.720 --> 09:30.900
So, I still need to say origin main.

09:30.900 --> 09:33.363
If I had used -u I could just say git push.

09:34.590 --> 09:37.980
So, actually it might just figure it out on its own,

09:37.980 --> 09:39.270
no it does not.

09:39.270 --> 09:42.303
Okay, so git push origin main.

09:46.479 --> 09:48.720
And if you have questions about that -u

09:48.720 --> 09:50.640
there's a standalone video I made on it

09:50.640 --> 09:52.560
so you could go check that out,

09:52.560 --> 09:54.203
but you probably already know that.

09:55.053 --> 09:57.090
Okay, and there we are.

09:57.090 --> 10:00.870
So, we see that we have this new commit one minute ago,

10:00.870 --> 10:05.250
less than that, where we merged movies and foods into main.

10:05.250 --> 10:09.090
And on main we see all three on GitHub.

10:09.090 --> 10:10.920
Foods just has the foods,

10:10.920 --> 10:14.086
and movies just has the movies.

10:14.086 --> 10:17.670
Okay, I need to take a break and watch one of these,

10:17.670 --> 10:19.800
that would be nice, with some peppermint ice cream

10:19.800 --> 10:22.290
and pretzels and not celery.

10:22.290 --> 10:24.783
I don't like celery at all really, bye-bye.
